      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Collect TikTok transcripts by hashtag with Apify\n\n### Who's it for\n\nContent creators, social media marketers, and researchers who want to understand why TikTok videos go viral by studying what people actually say, not just the caption or metadata.\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow is manually triggered, sets a list of hashtags to search, and sends them to an Apify actor to collect matching data. It then extracts each transcript URL from the actor results, downloads the transcript file, filters the downloaded items, and converts the remaining data into a file output.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Apify credentials in n8n and select the correct actor in the \"Run an Actor and get dataset\" node.\n- Update the \"Set hashtags to search\" node with the hashtags or search terms you want to process.\n- Verify that the Apify actor output contains the transcript URL field expected by the \"Extract transcript URL\" node.\n- Adjust the \"Filter\" node conditions so only the desired transcript items are converted to a file.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can change the hashtag list, swap the Apify actor, modify the transcript URL extraction expression, or alter the final file format and filter rules."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "37cecaa7-ae03-4dfa-92b2-b9a80fbf6ce1",
